# Implementation Plan — Enterprise Digital Asset Management (DAM) Refactoring Guide

## Overview
This document provides a comprehensive technical architecture and execution plan for refactoring the application to a centralized **Enterprise Digital Asset Management (DAM)** architecture backed by **Supabase Storage** and PostgreSQL metadata, while **preserving 100% of existing UI/UX**.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **Zero UI/UX Changes:** Existing upload dialogs, drag-and-drop zones, progress bars, popover menus, and audio playback controls remain visually unchanged.
> - **Binary Removal:** No business entity will store raw Base64 strings, byte arrays, or Blob data in database properties (e.g. `audioData` in `MeetingNotesBlock` is replaced by DAM `fileId` references).
> - **Single Upload Pipeline:** Every file upload flows strictly through `FileService.upload()` with zero direct component calls to storage buckets.
> - **Supabase Storage Integration:** Physical files are stored securely in Supabase Storage (`enterprise-assets` bucket) with Row Level Security (RLS) and signed URLs.

---

## Detailed Implementation Plan (10 Points)

### Point 1: Primary Objective & Binary Removal Architecture (`TASK-DAM-001`)
- Refactor all business records (`ddata`, `MeetingNotesBlock`, `UploadZone`, record attachments) to eliminate raw binary/Base64/Blob storage.
- Business entities persist only `fileId` (UUID) references or array of `fileId`s.
- Existing binary properties (e.g. `audioData`, `base64Data`) will be migrated into Supabase Storage physical assets and referenced via `fileId`.

### Point 2: Preserve Existing UI/UX (`TASK-DAM-002`)
- Keep all existing React UI components (`MeetingNotesBlock.jsx`, `UploadZone.jsx`, `ConfigurableListTemplate.tsx`) visually identical.
- Refactor only the asynchronous handlers called after the user selects or drops a file.

### Point 3: Single Upload Pipeline Abstraction (`FileService.upload`) (`TASK-DAM-003`)
- Create centralized client service `FileService` at `src/services/FileService.ts`:
  ```typescript
  export interface UploadParams {
    file: File | Blob;
    entityType: string;
    entityId: string;
    objectId?: string;
    ownerId?: string;
    metadata?: Record<string, any>;
    options?: {
      generateThumbnail?: boolean;
      extractMetadata?: boolean;
      isPublic?: boolean;
    };
  }

  export class FileService {
    static async upload(params: UploadParams): Promise<{ fileId: string; publicUrl?: string }>;
  }
  ```
- Components will never access Supabase directly, calculate storage paths, or generate bucket names.

### Point 4: Target Architecture & End-to-End Layer Flow (`TASK-DAM-004`)
- Flow: `React UI` -> `FileService.upload()` -> `Client Validation` -> `Metadata Extraction & Checksum` -> `Supabase Storage (Physical)` -> `enterprise_files (Metadata)` -> Return `fileId` -> Business entity saves `fileId`.

### Point 5: Client & Server Validation Framework (`TASK-DAM-005`)
- Enforce strict validation rules on both frontend and server:
  - Allowed file extensions & MIME type matching.
  - Maximum size limits by file type (Images: 20MB, Audio: 100MB, Video: 500MB, Docs: 50MB).
  - Audio/Video duration sanity checks.
  - SHA-256 duplicate file detection.

### Point 6: Dynamic File Processing & Type-Specific Pipelines (`TASK-DAM-006`)
- **Images:** Width, height, aspect ratio, orientation, EXIF, thumbnail generation.
- **PDFs:** Page count, preview rendering, OCR hook.
- **Office Docs:** Author, title, creation date, modification audit.
- **Audio:** Duration, sample rate, channels, codec, waveform JSON generation, Ziva AI transcript hook.
- **Video:** Duration, resolution, frame rate, video codec, poster thumbnail extraction.

### Point 7: Enterprise Digital Asset Schema (`enterprise_files` Table) (`TASK-DAM-007`)
- Create SQL migration for `enterprise_files` based on `Enterprise_Digital_Asset_Table_v1`:
  - Columns: `id` (UUID PK), `file_name`, `original_name`, `file_extension`, `mime_type`, `size_bytes`, `storage_bucket`, `storage_path`, `checksum_sha256`, `owner_id`, `tenant_id`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `is_deleted`.
  - JSONB Metadata Columns: `physical_metadata`, `version_info`, `status_info`, `security_info`, `ai_metadata`, `search_metadata`, `processing_metadata`, `audit_info`, `custom_metadata`, `system_metadata`, `compliance_metadata`.

### Point 8: Repository Migration Inventory (`TASK-DAM-008`)
- **Location 1:** `MeetingNotesBlock.jsx` -> Refactor `audioData` Base64 string & `audioFiles` array to store `fileId` references retrieved from `FileService.upload()`.
- **Location 2:** `UploadZone.jsx` -> Refactor local FileReader Base64 preview to call `FileService.upload()`.
- **Location 3:** `ConfigurableListTemplate.tsx` -> Refactor list record file attachments to DAM `fileId` pattern.
- **Location 4:** Record attachments (`RecordsList.tsx`, `RecordDetail.tsx`) -> Store DAM `fileId` instead of inline byte arrays.

### Point 9: Centralized `FileService` Implementation (`TASK-DAM-009`)
- Implement complete API surface in `FileService`:
  - `upload(params)`
  - `download(fileId)`
  - `getSignedUrl(fileId, expiresInSeconds)`
  - `delete(fileId, softDelete)`
  - `restore(fileId)`
  - `getMetadata(fileId)`
  - `listForEntity(entityType, entityId)`

### Point 10: Supabase Storage, Security Policies & AI Enrichment Hooks (`TASK-DAM-010`)
- Setup `enterprise-assets` bucket in Supabase Storage.
- Apply Row Level Security (RLS) policies for multi-tenant isolation.
- Integrate AI enrichment hooks for Ziva AI audio transcription, OCR, and semantic vector embeddings.

